class.description:
[InputMapSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"input_map"[/code]: it stores the keys, mouse buttons and joypad inputs the player bound to the actions of the project, loads them when the game starts and applies them to [InputMap] (in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], before the [SceneTree] exists). Sensitivity, inversion, vibration and the global deadzone are a separate domain, see [InputSettingsServer].
An event slot is addressed by action, device ([enum InputAction.InputDevice]: keyboard, mouse or gamepad) and slot. Slot [code]n[/code] of a device is the [code]n[/code]-th event of that device in the action. A rebinding menu with the columns "Keyboard 1", "Keyboard 2" and "Gamepad" waits for the next input of the player and calls [method rebind] with the slot of the column; the device follows from the event. [method clear_event] removes the event of a slot, and the later slots of that device move up. [method find_conflicts] tells which other actions use the event already, so the game can swap, clear or refuse. [method get_event_label] gives the text for the buttons of the menu.
The settings resource is an [InputActions] with one [InputAction] per action; the key of an entry is [member InputAction.action]. The defaults are the [InputMap] of the project settings when the game starts, so [method reset_action] and [method reset_all] give back the bindings of the project. [member save_mode] decides which actions are managed: only the custom actions of the project by default, or the built-in [code]ui_*[/code] actions too (see [constant InputMap.INPUT_ACTION_LAYER_CUSTOM]).
When the file is loaded, the saved actions replace the bindings of their action. Actions added to the project since the file was saved keep their project bindings; saved actions that the project no longer has are skipped with a warning. Applying replaces the key, mouse button and joypad events of each action; other event types (touch, MIDI, ...) stay. An action that the player cleared is saved with its remaining events, so the project binding does not come back.
The file is [code]user://settings/input_map.ini[/code] by default and stores every action as a record and every event as a record with named fields, not as [InputEvent] sub-resources: [member InputMapSettingsAction.deadzone] and [member InputMapSettingsAction.input_events] per action; [member InputMapSettingsEvent.device] ([code]Keyboard[/code], [code]Mouse[/code], [code]Gamepad[/code]), [member InputMapSettingsEvent.input] ([code]W[/code], [code]Space[/code], [code]Left[/code], [code]WheelUp[/code], [code]A[/code], [code]LeftStickLeft[/code], [code]RightTrigger[/code], ...; a gamepad axis has its direction in the name), [member InputMapSettingsEvent.modifiers] ([code]Ctrl+Shift[/code]), [member InputMapSettingsEvent.key_mode] ([code]Physical[/code], [code skip-lint]Label[/code] or [code skip-lint]Printed[/code], keyboard only) and [member InputMapSettingsEvent.device_id] ([code]Any[/code] or a joypad number) per event. JSON, YAML, TOML and XML nest the events in their action; INI writes a section per action and per event; CSV has one row per event with the columns [code]action[/code], [code]index[/code], [code]device[/code], [code]input[/code], [code]modifiers[/code], [code]key_mode[/code], [code]device_id[/code] and [code]deadzone[/code] (an action without events is one row with an empty [code]input[/code]). The events of the settings are always in a canonical form (one key code, all devices or one joypad), so an action read back from the file equals the action that was saved. Files of version 2 (one text cell [code]bindings[/code] per action, such as [code]Key:Ctrl+S; JoypadButton:A[/code]) and of version 1 are still read; version 1 files in XML, TOML and YAML give their actions the project bindings until the next save.
All methods below change the pending settings: in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE] a change reaches [InputMap] at once and is saved at the end of the frame; in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL] it waits for [method SettingsServer.apply].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var waiting_action = &""
var waiting_slot = 0

func _on_jump_key_button_pressed():
	waiting_action = &"jump"
	waiting_slot = 0

func _input(event):
	if waiting_action.is_empty() or not event.is_pressed():
		return
	if InputAction.get_event_device(event) == InputAction.INPUT_DEVICE_MAX:
		return # Mouse motion, touch, ...
	get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()
	for other in InputMapSettingsServer.find_conflicts(event, waiting_action):
		InputMapSettingsServer.remove_event(other, event)
	InputMapSettingsServer.rebind(waiting_action, event, waiting_slot)
	$JumpKeyButton.text = InputMapSettingsServer.get_event_label(event)
	waiting_action = &""
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private StringName _waitingAction = "";
private int _waitingSlot = 0;

private void OnJumpKeyButtonPressed()
{
    _waitingAction = "jump";
    _waitingSlot = 0;
}

public override void _Input(InputEvent @event)
{
    if (_waitingAction.IsEmpty || !@event.IsPressed())
    {
        return;
    }
    if (InputAction.GetEventDevice(@event) == InputAction.InputDevice.Max)
    {
        return; // Mouse motion, touch, ...
    }
    GetViewport().SetInputAsHandled();
    foreach (string other in InputMapSettingsServer.FindConflicts(@event, _waitingAction))
    {
        InputMapSettingsServer.RemoveEvent(other, @event);
    }
    InputMapSettingsServer.Rebind(_waitingAction, @event, _waitingSlot);
    GetNode<Button>("JumpKeyButton").Text = InputMapSettingsServer.GetEventLabel(@event);
    _waitingAction = "";
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
